pred DE table omits 14 of the 42260 reference-significant (target, feature) pairs (0.033%), across 9 of 32 target(s); worst is 'DNMT1' with 5. An omitted pair never enters the direction metrics' ranking pool -- it neither advances the purity depth nor counts as a miss -- while still counting in N_conf, so the eleven target-excluding direction metrics (including the two vcc2026 scores among them) can read differently from a table covering the reference's whole confident budget. The effect is NOT one-directional: omitting head-ranked misses can inflate direction_reach_raw, while omitting correct calls or absorbable tail misses can lower it. Counts are for THIS prepared DE slice (issue #291).
